===Licensing agreement with Marvel Studios===
<!--Please do not change this heading! This is correct because the section covers both the info leading to the deal AND the films-->
[[File:Spider-Man (Marvel Cinematic Universe) film logo.png|thumb|upright=1.4|right|alt=Logo for the MCU Spider-Man franchise|Franchise logo from 2017 to 2021]]

Marvel had been seeking to incorporate Spider-Man into their multimedia franchise, the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] (MCU), as early as 2014.<ref name="FeigeCraveApril2015">{{Cite web |url=http://www.craveonline.com/film/articles/845723 |title=Exclusive: Marvel's Spider-Man Reboot is NOT an Origin Story |website=[[CraveOnline]] |date=April 11, 2015 |access-date=April 11, 2015 |last=Bibbiani |first=William |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150416171939/http://www.craveonline.com/film/articles/845723 |archive-date=April 16, 2015 |url-status=dead }}</ref> By this point, they were pursuing control of the film rights thanks to their recent box office success.<ref name="WSJDealNumbers">{{Cite web |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/spider-man-a-175-million-commercial-for-disney-toys-1498815005 |title='Spider-Man:' A $175 Million Commercial for Disney Toys |last=Fritz |first=Ben |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |date=June 30, 2017 |access-date=August 28, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170702010902/https://www.wsj.com/articles/spider-man-a-175-million-commercial-for-disney-toys-1498815005 |archive-date=July 2, 2017 |url-status=dead<!-- Full article available via the archive, even if link is still live--> |url-access=subscription}}<!-- Transcript of article available on [http://pasted.co/68f54d81 Pasted.co]--></ref> Studio president [[Kevin Feige]] suggested [[Retroactive continuity|retroactively]] integrating ''The Amazing Spider-Man'' franchise into the MCU to [[Amy Pascal]], then-Sony co-chairman, to improve the prospects of associated films.<ref name=varietyintegration>{{cite magazine | author=Selome Hailu | url=https://variety.com/2021/film/news/kevin-feige-amy-pascal-spider-man-mcu-1235137818/ | title=Kevin Feige and Amy Pascal Discuss Their Future ‘Spider-Man’ Plans: ‘We Want to Top Ourselves in Quality and Emotion’ | magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] | date=December 18, 2021 | access-date=August 28, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250828161759/https://variety.com/2021/film/news/kevin-feige-amy-pascal-spider-man-mcu-1235137818/|archive-date=August 28, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=nytintegration>{{cite news |url= https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/17/movies/kevin-feige-amy-pascal-spider-man-no-way-home.html |title= Kevin Feige and Amy Pascal on the Future of ‘Spider-Man’ and the M.C.U. |first=Brooks |last=Barnes |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=December 17, 2021 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20250815213733/https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/17/movies/kevin-feige-amy-pascal-spider-man-no-way-home.html |archive-date=August 15, 2025|url-status=live|url-access=subscription|access-date=August 28, 2025}}</ref> At the same time, Pascal and producer [[Avi Arad]] had attempted to establish continuity by authorizing use of the design of ''The Amazing Spider-Man''{{'s}} Oscorp Tower for ''[[The Avengers (2012 film)|The Avengers]]'' (2012), but the approval process occurred too late into the production of ''The Avengers''.<ref>{{cite web|last=Collura|first=Scott|title=A Spider-Man/Avengers Crossover Almost Happened|work=[[IGN]]|date=June 15, 2012|url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2012/06/15/a-spider-manavengers-crossover-almost-happened|access-date=November 25, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250828171251/https://www.ign.com/articles/2012/06/15/a-spider-manavengers-crossover-almost-happened|archive-date=August 28, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Another idea brought forward was a [[crossover (fiction)|crossover]] film combining ''The Amazing Spider-Man'' universe with that of the Raimi trilogy.<ref name=sonywallstreet>{{cite news |url= https://www.wsj.com/articles/BL-SEB-85444 |title= Sony, Marvel Discussed Spider-Man Movie Crossover |first=Ben |last=Fritz |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |date=December 9, 2014 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20160330095714/http://blogs.wsj.com/speakeasy/2014/12/09/sony-marvel-discussed-spider-man-movie-crossover/ |archive-date=March 30, 2016|url-status=live|url-access=subscription|access-date=August 28, 2025}}</ref> 

In December 2014, an anonymous group [[2014 Sony Pictures hack|hacked Sony's computer networks and leaked confidential information]], among them emails of discussions between Sony and Marvel pertaining to the licensing of Spider-Man for the MCU film ''[[Captain America: Civil War]]'' (2016).<ref name=sonywallstreet/> Negotiations over the copyrights stalled until Disney and Sony brokered an agreement in February 2015.<ref name=sonywallstreet2>{{cite news |url= http://www.wsj.com/articles/marvel-and-sony-reach-deal-on-spider-man-movie-production-1423546677|title=Marvel and Sony Reach Deal on Spider-Man Movie Production |first=Ben |last=Fritz |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |date=February 9, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150211024143/http://www.wsj.com/articles/marvel-and-sony-reach-deal-on-spider-man-movie-production-1423546677 |archive-date=February 11, 2015|url-status=live|url-access=subscription|access-date=August 28, 2025}}</ref><ref name="SpideyMCU">{{cite web|url=https://news.marvel.com/movies/24062/sony_pictures_entertainment_brings_marvel_studios_into_the_amazing_world_of_spider-man/ |title=Sony Pictures Entertainment Brings Marvel Studios Into The Amazing World Of Spider-Man|publisher=[[Marvel Entertainment]]|date=February 9, 2015|access-date=February 10, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170618065904/https://news.marvel.com/movies/24062/sony_pictures_entertainment_brings_marvel_studios_into_the_amazing_world_of_spider-man/|archive-date=June 18, 2017|url-status=dead}}</ref> It reinstated the conditions of their preexisting arrangement, with a clause that entitled Marvel the right to reduce their annual [[royalty payment]]s to Sony based on the performance of their films.<ref name="WSJDealNumbers"/><ref name="SonyNoPlaybook">{{Cite web |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=August 21, 2019 |title='Spider-Man' Standoff: Why Sony Thinks It Doesn't Need "Kevin's Playbook" Anymore |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/spider-man-standoff-why-sony-thinks-it-doesnt-need-kevins-playbook-anymore-1233644 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190822180352/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/spider-man-standoff-why-sony-thinks-it-doesnt-need-kevins-playbook-anymore-1233644 |archive-date=August 22, 2019 |access-date=August 28, 2025 |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> Conversely, Sony retained full creative control of the MCU Spider-Man films.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Sony Pictures Entertainment Brings Marvel Studios Into The Amazing World Of Spider-Man {{!}} Sony Pictures Entertainment |url=https://www.sonypictures.com/corp/press_releases/2015/02_15/020915_spiderman.html|access-date=March 1, 2026 |publisher=[[Sony Pictures Entertainment]]|date=February 9, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260115101803/https://www.sonypictures.com/corp/press_releases/2015/02_15/020915_spiderman.html|archive-date=January 15, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref>

The studios once more renegotiated in 2019, briefly resulting in the dissolution of their partnership.<ref name="NoNewDealSonyResponse">{{Cite web |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=August 20, 2019 |title='Spider-Man' Studio Sony Goes Public with Marvel Movie Divorce: "We Are Disappointed" (Exclusive) |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/sony-fires-back-at-marvel-spider-man-movie-divorce-1233490 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190821071513/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/sony-fires-back-at-marvel-spider-man-movie-divorce-1233490 |archive-date=August 21, 2019 |access-date=August 21, 2019 |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> Sony sought to maintain their original agreement, which conferred merchandising rights and 5% of [[first-dollar gross]] to Disney.<ref name="NoNewSonyDealAug2019THR">{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/sony-marvel-split-future-spider-man-releases-1233383/|title=Sony, Marvel to Split on Future 'Spider-Man' Releases|last1=Kit|first1=Borys|last2=McMillian|first2=Graeme|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=August 20, 2019|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190820215052/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/sony-marvel-split-future-spider-man-releases-1233383|archive-date=August 20, 2019|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="NoNewSonyDealAug2019Variety">{{cite web |url=https://variety.com/2019/film/news/spider-man-mcu-sony-disney-agreement-1203308069/|title=Spider-Man Could Leave MCU if Disney, Sony Can't Reach Financing Deal|last=McNary|first=Dave|work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=August 20, 2019|access-date=August 20, 2019|archive-date=August 20, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190820214857/https://variety.com/2019/film/news/spider-man-mcu-sony-disney-agreement-1203308069/|url-status=live}}</ref> On the other hand, Disney demanded that future Spider-Man films produced by Feige be funded equally in a cooperative venture, increasing their share of profits.<ref name="NoNewSonyDealAug2019">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2019/08/kevin-feige-spider-man-franchise-exit-disney-sony-dispute-avengers-endgame-captain-america-winter-soldier-tom-rothman-bob-iger-1202672545/|title=Disney-Sony Standoff Ends Marvel Studios & Kevin Feige's Involvement In 'Spider-Man'|last=Fleming|first=Mike Jr.|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=August 20, 2019|access-date=August 20, 2019|url-status=live|archive-date=August 20, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190820201532/https://deadline.com/2019/08/kevin-feige-spider-man-franchise-exit-disney-sony-dispute-avengers-endgame-captain-america-winter-soldier-tom-rothman-bob-iger-1202672545/}}</ref> Negotiations resumed after public backlash, and the studios reached a new deal that September, the terms of which guaranteed a third Spider-Man film and a related MCU project.<ref name="DeadlineSonyMarvelDealSM3">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=September 27, 2019 |title=Spider-Man Back in Action As Sony Agrees To Disney Co-Fi For New Movie, Return To MCU: How Spidey's Web Got Untangled |url=https://deadline.com/2019/09/sony-walt-disneys-marvel-team-on-third-spider-man-homecoming-title-with-superhero-to-appear-in-future-marvel-pics-1202746497/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190927174504/https://deadline.com/2019/09/sony-walt-disneys-marvel-team-on-third-spider-man-homecoming-title-with-superhero-to-appear-in-future-marvel-pics-1202746497/ |archive-date=September 27, 2019 |access-date=August 28, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref name="DisneySonySpidey3">{{Cite web |url=https://variety.com/2019/film/news/sony-marvel-tom-holland-spider-man-1203351489/ |title=Sony, Marvel Make Up: Companies Will Produce Third 'Spider-Man' Film |last=Lang |first=Brent |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |date=September 27, 2019 |access-date=September 27, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190927160452/https://variety.com/2019/film/news/sony-marvel-tom-holland-spider-man-1203351489/ |archive-date=September 27, 2019 |url-status=live}}</ref>

===Title roles===
====''Spider-Man: Homecoming'' (2017)====
{{main|Spider-Man: Homecoming|l1 = ''Spider-Man: Homecoming''}}

[[File:Tom Holland (28652884235) (cropped).jpg|thumb|upright|alt=Cropped photo of Tom Holland at the 2016 San Diego Comic Con International|[[Tom Holland]] in 2016|left]]

Work on an MCU Spider-Man production began in February 2015.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2015/02/spider-man-marvel-kevin-feige-amy-pascal-producers-1201370228/|title=‘Spider-Man’ Scoop: Marvel’s Kevin Feige, Amy Pascal To Steer Spidey As Producers|last=Fleming|first=Mike Jr.|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=February 9, 2015|access-date=September 2, 2025|url-status=live|archive-date=September 1, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250901052838/https://deadline.com/2015/02/spider-man-marvel-kevin-feige-amy-pascal-producers-1201370228/}}</ref> [[Ted Melfi]], [[Jonathan Levine]], and [[Jon Watts]] were among the filmmakers executives considered to direct ''Spider-Man: Homecoming'', with Watts ultimately signed as director in June 2015.<ref name="THRCastingSecrets"/> Watts came to Marvel's attention for his work in the independent thriller ''[[Cop Car (film)|Cop Car]]'' (2015).<ref name=iw1>{{Cite web |last= England |first=Kate |date=July 5, 2017 |title= ‘Spider-Man: Homecoming’: How a Sundance Breakout Landed the Superhero Gig of a Lifetime and Didn’t Sell Out |url= https://www.indiewire.com/features/general/spider-man-homecoming-tom-holland-jon-watts-interview-1201849260/ |url-status=live |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20250901052140/https://www.indiewire.com/features/general/spider-man-homecoming-tom-holland-jon-watts-interview-1201849260/ |archive-date=September 1, 2025 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[IndieWire]]}}</ref> The studios hired a succession of writers to produce the script for ''Homecoming''.<ref name="SDCC2016">{{cite web|url=http://marvel.com/news/movies/26510/sdcc_2016_spider-man_homecoming_introduces_its_villain|title=SDCC 2016: 'Spider-Man: Homecoming' Introduces Its Villain|last=Strom|first=Marc|publisher=[[Marvel Entertainment]]|date=July 23, 2016|access-date=July 23, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180612142448/http://marvel.com/news/movies/26510/sdcc_2016_spider-man_homecoming_introduces_its_villain|archive-date=June 12, 2018|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name=homecomingew>{{cite web |url=https://ew.com/movies/2017/08/02/spider-man-homecoming-writers-answer-burning-questions/ |title=Spider-Man: Homecoming writers answer some burning questions|last=Vilkomerson |first=Sara|work=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|date=August 2, 2017|access-date=September 2, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250901032139/https://ew.com/movies/2017/08/02/spider-man-homecoming-writers-answer-burning-questions/|archive-date=September 1, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> 

Some 1,500 actors were scouted for the role of [[Peter Parker (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Peter Parker / Spider-Man]].<ref name="SpideyCastingCall" /> Six of the actors auditioned in screen tests with [[Robert Downey Jr.]] in character as [[Iron Man|Iron Man / Tony Stark]], which the producers viewed to observe their onscreen chemistry.<ref name="THRCastingSecrets">{{cite web |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/how-new-spider-man-team-804569/|title=Robert Downey Jr. and Secret Screen-Tests: How the New 'Spider-Man' Team Was Chosen|last1=Kit|first1=Borys |last2=Siegel |first2=Tatiana|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=June 23, 2015|access-date=April 21, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220413213616/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/how-new-spider-man-team-804569/|archive-date=April 13, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="SpideyCastingCall">{{cite web |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/spider-man-hopefuls-screen-test-798995/ |title=Spider-Man Hopefuls Screen-Test in Atlanta as Marvel Decision Nears (Exclusive)|last=Kit|first=Borys |work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=May 30, 2015|access-date=May 30, 2015|archive-date=June 23, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150623143635/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/spider-man-hopefuls-screen-test-798995|url-status=live}}</ref> The filmmakers held further auditions when [[Tom Holland]] and [[Charlie Rowe]] were picked as the finalists.<ref name="THRCastingSecrets" /> Holland was cast as Peter in June 2015, signing a six-picture deal to appear in three Spider-Man films and three other MCU films.<ref name=MarvelSonyJune23>{{cite web|title=Sony Pictures and Marvel Studios Find Their 'Spider-Man' Star and Director|url=http://marvel.com/news/movies/24758/sony_pictures_and_marvel_studios_find_their_spider-man_star_and_director|date=June 23, 2015|access-date=June 24, 2015|archive-date=June 24, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150624232902/http://marvel.com/news/movies/24758/sony_pictures_and_marvel_studios_find_their_spider-man_star_and_director|url-status=deviated |publisher=[[Marvel Entertainment]]}}</ref><ref name="HollandContract">{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/tom-holland-his-spider-man-incarnation-time-see-kid-945320/|title=Tom Holland Learned He Got His 'Spider-Man: Homecoming' Role From a Marvel Instagram Post|last=Siegel|first=Tatiana|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=November 9, 2016|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220412125428/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/tom-holland-his-spider-man-incarnation-time-see-kid-945320/|archive-date=April 12, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Homecoming'' details Peter's transformation into Spider-Man, in what the filmmakers described as a [[coming-of-age story]].<ref name=iw1/><ref name=homecomingew/> Shooting took place from June to October 2016,<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2016/06/20/chris-pratt-tom-holland-james-gunn-spider-man-homecoming |title=Chris Pratt, Tom Holland cross paths as Spider-Man: Homecoming starts filming|last=Coggan |first=Devan|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|date=June 20, 2016|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220413213559/https://ew.com/article/2016/06/20/chris-pratt-tom-holland-james-gunn-spider-man-homecoming/|archive-date=April 13, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.11alive.com/article/news/captain-america-civil-war-was-shot-in-around-atlanta/85-170019060|title="Captain America: Civil War" was shot in, around Atlanta|last=Leslie|first=Jennifer|publisher=[[WXIA-TV]]|date=May 5, 2016|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=|archive-date=|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://ew.com/article/2016/10/03/spider-man-homecoming-tom-holland-announces-filming-wrapped/ |title=Spider-Man: Homecoming: Tom Holland announces filming has wrapped|last=Derschowitz |first=Jessica|work=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|date=October 3, 2016|access-date=September 2, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250901053945/https://ew.com/article/2016/10/03/spider-man-homecoming-tom-holland-announces-filming-wrapped/|archive-date=September 1, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> and the film was released in July 2017.<ref>{{cite web|last=Ford|first=Rebecca|date=January 20, 2016|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/jumanji-release-date-pushed-spider-man-shifts-857644/|title='Jumanji' Release Date Pushed, 'Spider-Man' Shifts Up|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220413213556/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/jumanji-release-date-pushed-spider-man-shifts-857644/|archive-date=April 13, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> 

====''Spider-Man: Far From Home'' (2019)====
{{main|Spider-Man: Far From Home|l1 = ''Spider-Man: Far From Home''}}

Studio executives were already contemplating sequels to ''Homecoming'' before the original film's release.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Galloway |first=Stephen |date=June 23, 2016 |title=Tom Rothman on ''Spider-Man'' Plans and Loving ''Ghostbusters'' Trolls: 'Can We Please Get Some More Haters to Say Stupid Things?' |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/tom-rothman-spider-man-plans-904849 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160624080219/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/tom-rothman-spider-man-plans-904849 |archive-date=June 24, 2016 |access-date=September 2, 2025|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Nordstrom |first=Leigh |date=October 16, 2016 |title=Robert Pattinson, Sienna Miller Talk ''The Lost City of Z'' |url=http://wwd.com/eye/parties/robert-pattinson-sienna-miller-new-york-film-festival-the-lost-city-of-z-10676426/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161018171214/http://wwd.com/eye/parties/robert-pattinson-sienna-miller-new-york-film-festival-the-lost-city-of-z-10676426/ |archive-date=October 18, 2016 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[Women's Wear Daily]]}}</ref> The filmmakers developed ''Spider-Man: Far From Home'' as the final film of the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe: Phase Three|third phase]] of the MCU's Infinity Saga.<ref>{{cite web|last=Sharf |first=Zack |date=April 22, 2019 |title=MCU Timeline Shifts as 'Spider Man: Far From Home' Confirmed as Phase Three Finale, Not 'Endgame' |url=https://www.indiewire.com/2019/04/kevin-feige-spider-man-far-from-home-mcu-phase-three-end-1202126755/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210603215447/https://www.indiewire.com/2019/04/kevin-feige-spider-man-far-from-home-mcu-phase-three-end-1202126755/ |archive-date=June 3, 2021 |access-date=June 3, 2021 |website=[[IndieWire]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/spider-man-far-from-home-infinity-saga-end|title=Kevin Feige Explains Why Spider-Man: Far From Home Wraps Up MCU's Infinity Saga|last=Weiss|first=Josh|website=[[Syfy]]|date=June 24, 2019|access-date=September 2, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250901160108/https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/spider-man-far-from-home-infinity-saga-end|archive-date=September 1, 2025}}</ref> Watts and screenwriters [[Chris McKenna (writer)|Chris McKenna]] and [[Erik Sommers]] were confirmed to be returning for the film in mid 2017.<ref>{{cite web|last=Courtney |first=Amanda |date=July 19, 2017 |title=Director Jon Watts Returning for Spider-Man: Homecoming Sequel |url=https://www.motionpictures.org/2017/07/director-jon-watts-returning-spider-man-homecoming-sequel/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251011101443/https://www.motionpictures.org/2017/07/director-jon-watts-returning-spider-man-homecoming-sequel/|archive-date=October 11, 2025 |access-date=January 25, 2026 |publisher=[[Motion Picture Association]]}}</ref><ref name="McKennaSommers">{{Cite web |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=August 30, 2017 |title=''Spider-Man: Homecoming'' Writers Returning for Sequel (Exclusive) |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/spider-man-homecoming-writers-returning-sequel-1033928 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170831002607/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/spider-man-homecoming-writers-returning-sequel-1033928 |archive-date=August 31, 2017 |access-date=August 30, 2017 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> Watts was especially interested in resolving the narratives about the Spider-Man characters from ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]'' (2019) because they received an ambiguous resolution.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Coogan |first=Devan |date=May 6, 2019 |title=''Spider-Man: Far From Home'' director Jon Watts breaks down that post-''Endgame'' trailer |url=https://ew.com/movies/2019/05/06/spider-man-far-from-home-director-breaks-down-that-post-endgame-trailer-exclusive/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190508011331/https://ew.com/movies/2019/05/06/spider-man-far-from-home-director-breaks-down-that-post-endgame-trailer-exclusive/ |archive-date=May 8, 2019 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> In ''Far From Home'', [[Nick Fury (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Nick Fury]] ([[Samuel L. Jackson]]) recruits Peter to help [[Mysterio (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Mysterio]] ([[Jake Gyllenhaal]]) defeat the [[Elementals (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Elementals]]. Filming occurred from July to October 2018,<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/what-we-know-about-spider-man-homecoming-sequel-far-from-home-2018-6|title=All the details we know about the "Spider-Man: Homecoming" sequel, whose title was just revealed|last=Clark|first=Travis|work=[[Business Insider]]|access-date=January 25, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230422090047/https://www.businessinsider.com/what-we-know-about-spider-man-homecoming-sequel-far-from-home-2018-6|archive-date=April 22, 2023|date=June 25, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Romano |first=Nick |date=October 17, 2018 |title=Spider-Man: Far From Home wraps filming with new photos of the suit |url=https://ew.com/movies/2018/10/17/spider-man-far-from-home-filming-wrap/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230523080855/https://ew.com/movies/2018/10/17/spider-man-far-from-home-filming-wrap/ |archive-date=May 23, 2023 |access-date=January 25, 2026 |website=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> and the theatrical release was scheduled in July 2019.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2019/film/news/spider-man-far-from-home-trailer-sony-record-1203112547/|title=Film News Roundup: ‘Spider-Man: Far From Home’ Trailer Sets Sony Pictures Record |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|last=McNary|first=Dave|date=January 18, 2019|access-date=January 25, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240811033616/https://variety.com/2019/film/news/spider-man-far-from-home-trailer-sony-record-1203112547/|archive-date=August 11, 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Far From Home'' became the first Spider-Man film to gross $1{{nbsp}}billion at the box office.<ref name="BillionTheWrap">{{Cite web |last=Fuster |first=Jeremy |date=July 25, 2019 |title=''Spider-Man: Far From Home'' Becomes First Spidey Film to Gross $1 Billion at Box Office |url=https://www.thewrap.com/spider-man-far-from-home-1-billion/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220106092530/https://www.thewrap.com/spider-man-far-from-home-1-billion/ |archive-date=January 6, 2022 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref>

====''Spider-Man: No Way Home'' (2021)====
{{main|Spider-Man: No Way Home|l1 = ''Spider-Man: No Way Home''}}

A third entry in the MCU Spider-Man franchise began development shortly after Sony and Marvel's contract was effective.<ref name="DisneySonySpidey3"/> Watts continued his duties as director,<ref name="Foxx">{{Cite web |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=October 1, 2020 |title='Spider-Man 3' Jolt: Jamie Foxx Returning as Electro (Exclusive) |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/spider-man-3-jolt-jamie-foxx-returning-as-electro-exclusive |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201006025949/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/spider-man-3-jolt-jamie-foxx-returning-as-electro-exclusive |archive-date=October 6, 2020 |access-date=October 8, 2020 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> while McKenna and Sommers returned to write the screenplay of what would become ''Spider-Man: No Way Home''.<ref name="WattsDeadlineAug2019">{{Cite web |last=Fleming |first=Mike Jr. |date=August 23, 2019 |title=Next Post-'Spider-Man' Skirmish For Sony & Disney: A Tug Of War Over 'Spider-Man' Helmer Jon Watts? |url=https://deadline.com/2019/08/spider-man-disney-marvel-sony-director-jon-watts-next-film-courtship-1202702851/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190824000254/https://deadline.com/2019/08/spider-man-disney-marvel-sony-director-jon-watts-next-film-courtship-1202702851/ |archive-date=August 24, 2019 |access-date=August 24, 2019 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The writers conceived a [[Multiverse (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|multiverse]] story from an idea inspired by the fantasy drama ''[[It's a Wonderful Life]]'' (1946), wherein Peter convinces [[Stephen Strange (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Dr. Stephen Strange]] ([[Benedict Cumberbatch]]) to reverse the events leading to the exposure of his identity as Spider-Man with a [[incantation|spell]].<ref name="McKennaSommers2">{{Cite web |last=Couch |first=Aaron |date=December 29, 2021 |title=How ‘Spider-Man: No Way Home’ Was “Shaped” by Its Secret Stars |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/spider-man-no-way-home-andrew-garfield-tobey-maguire-1235068153/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250901212433/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/spider-man-no-way-home-andrew-garfield-tobey-maguire-1235068153/ |archive-date=September 1, 2025 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> The film connects Sony's Spider-Man universes to the MCU and features several of the associated characters, including Maguire and Garfield's Spider-Men.<ref name="McKennaSommers2"/><ref>{{Cite web |last=Goslin |first=Austen |date=November 16, 2021 |title=Spider-Man: No Way Home trailer unleashes the multiverse of villains |url=https://www.polygon.com/22703064/spider-man-no-way-home-trailer |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211117040023/https://www.polygon.com/22703064/spider-man-no-way-home-trailer |archive-date=November 17, 2021 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[Polygon (website)|Polygon]]}}</ref><ref name="NWHPastVillains">{{Cite magazine |last=Coggan |first=Devan |date=November 16, 2021 |title=New ''Spider-Man: No Way Home'' trailer swings headfirst into the multiverse |url=https://ew.com/movies/spider-man-no-way-home-new-trailer/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211117024812/https://ew.com/movies/spider-man-no-way-home-new-trailer/ |archive-date=November 17, 2021 |access-date=November 16, 2021 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> ''No Way Home''{{'s}} production lasted from October 2020 to March 2021,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nugent |first=Annabel |date=December 30, 2021 |title= Spider-Man: Surprise actors did not sign on to No Way Home until halfway through filming |url=https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/films/news/spider-man-no-way-home-andrew-garfield-tobey-maguire-b1984293.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250901215917/https://www.the-independent.com/arts-entertainment/films/news/spider-man-no-way-home-andrew-garfield-tobey-maguire-b1984293.html |archive-date=September 1, 2025 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[The Independent]]}}</ref> and the film debuted in theaters in December 2021.<ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=December 20, 2021 |title=''Spider-Man: No Way Home'' Defeats ''Infinity War'' & Notches 2nd Highest Domestic Opening At The Box Office With $260M |url=https://deadline.com/2021/12/spider-man-no-way-home-50m-preview-easily-pandemic-record-all-time-for-sony-100m-friday-likely-1234898486/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220102130337/https://deadline.com/2021/12/spider-man-no-way-home-50m-preview-easily-pandemic-record-all-time-for-sony-100m-friday-likely-1234898486/ |archive-date=January 2, 2022 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> By the end of the global rollout, it became the [[2021 in film#Highest-grossing films|highest-grossing film of 2021]] with a box office take of $1.910{{nbsp}}billion.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2021 Worldwide Box Office |url=https://www.boxofficemojo.com/year/world/2021/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221002064559/https://www.boxofficemojo.com/year/world/2021/ |archive-date=October 2, 2022 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[Box Office Mojo]]}}</ref>{{efn-lr|group=nb|name=reissue|Excludes grosses from subsequent re-releases.}}

====''Spider-Man: Brand New Day'' (2026)====
{{main|Spider-Man: Brand New Day|l1 = ''Spider-Man: Brand New Day''}}

Pascal announced work on a second trilogy of MCU Spider-Man films in 2021.<ref name="PascalInterview">{{Cite web|url=https://www.fandango.com/movie-news/spider-man-no-way-home-producer-amy-pascal-reveals-more-about-the-historic-film-and-confirms-tom-hollands-future-as-spider-man-754461|title='Spider-Man: No Way Home' Producer Amy Pascal Reveals More About the Historic Film and Confirms Tom Holland's Future as Spider-Man|last=Davis|first=Eric|date=November 29, 2021|access-date=November 29, 2021|publisher=[[Fandango Media]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913014501/https://www.fandango.com/movie-news/spider-man-no-way-home-producer-amy-pascal-reveals-more-about-the-historic-film-and-confirms-tom-hollands-future-as-spider-man-754461|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live|language=en}}</ref> Although ''No Way Home'' had been Holland's final contracted standalone film as Spider-Man, the actor was confirmed to be reprising the role for ''Spider-Man: Brand New Day'' in 2024.<ref name="HollandSpideyFuture">{{Cite news |last=Weiss |first=Josh |date=February 25, 2021 |title='Spider-Man: No Way Home' is the end of Tom Holland's contract, but he's in no rush to retire |url=https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/spider-man-no-way-home-tom-holland-marvel-contract |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250114132617/https://www.syfy.com/syfy-wire/spider-man-no-way-home-tom-holland-marvel-contract |archive-date=January 14, 2025 |access-date=January 25, 2026 |work=[[Syfy Wire]]}}</ref><ref name="Spiderman4">{{Cite web |last=Dinsdale |first=Ryan |date=October 23, 2024 |title=Spider-Man 4 Confirmed at Marvel Studios, Tom Holland to Begin Filming in 2025 |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/spider-man-4-confirmed-at-marvel-studios-tom-holland-to-begin-filming-in-2025 |website=[[IGN]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913023007/https://www.ign.com/articles/spider-man-4-confirmed-at-marvel-studios-tom-holland-to-begin-filming-in-2025|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> The film was directed by [[Destin Daniel Cretton]].<ref name="Cretton">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=October 25, 2024|title=Sony Adds Untitled ''Spider-Man'' With Tom Holland To Summer 2026 Calendar; Destin Daniel Cretton Directing |url=https://deadline.com/2024/10/spider-man-tom-holland-new-movie-1236158673/|access-date=October 25, 2024|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913021518/https://deadline.com/2024/10/spider-man-tom-holland-new-movie-1236158673/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Principal photography was postponed to accommodate Holland's simultaneous commitments to ''[[Avengers: Doomsday]]'' and the [[Christopher Nolan]]-directed film [[The Odyssey (2026 film)|''The Odyssey'']] (both 2026).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=October 21, 2024|title=Tom Holland to Star in Christopher Nolan’s Latest Film |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/tom-holland-to-star-in-christopher-nolan-next-film-1236040294/ |access-date=October 26, 2024|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913015529/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/tom-holland-to-star-in-christopher-nolan-next-film-1236040294/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live|language=en-US}}</ref> ''Brand New Day''{{'s}} main story shows Peter adjusting to life in isolation and a set of grief-induced physiological changes that enhance his spider senses.<ref>{{cite web |last=Tallerico |first=Brian |date=July 28, 2026 |title=Spider-Man: Brand New Day|url=https://www.rogerebert.com/reviews/spider-man-brand-new-day-2026-movie-review|access-date=August 18, 2026 |publisher=[[RogerEbert.com]] |archive-date=August 8, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260808221416/https://www.rogerebert.com/reviews/spider-man-brand-new-day-2026-movie-review|url-status=live}}</ref> Following its July 2026 debut,<ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=February 21, 2025 |title=New Tom Holland 'Spider-Man' Going A Week Later In July 2026 |url=https://deadline.com/2025/02/tom-holland-spider-man-release-date-2026-1236297935/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250222001143/https://deadline.com/2025/02/tom-holland-spider-man-release-date-2026-1236297935/ |archive-date=February 22, 2025 |access-date=February 22, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Murphy |first=J. Kim |date=February 21, 2025 |title=Tom Holland's 'Spider-Man 4' Gets New July 2026 Release, Moves Two Weeks Out From Christopher Nolan's 'The Odyssey' |url=https://variety.com/2025/film/news/spider-man-4-delayed-two-weeks-tom-holland-nolan-odyssey-1236316067/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250222100000/https://variety.com/2025/film/news/spider-man-4-delayed-two-weeks-tom-holland-nolan-odyssey-1236316067/ |archive-date=February 22, 2025 |access-date=February 22, 2025 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> the [[Rotten Tomatoes]] consensus noted that the film "is a promising reset that portends Spidey will remain sticky on the big screen for years to come."<ref name=bnd/> ''Brand New Day'' broke multiple box office records and, at $2.517 billion as of October 2026, represents the [[2026 in film|highest-grossing film of the year]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=D'Alessandro |first1=Anthony |date=August 17, 2026 |title=‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’ Becomes Second-Fastest To Cross $2B WW – Global Top 10 Box Office Update |url=https://deadline.com/2026/08/box-office-global-spider-man-brand-new-day-2-1237042050/ |access-date=August 18, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |archive-date=August 18, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260818132556/https://deadline.com/2026/08/box-office-global-spider-man-brand-new-day-2-1237042050/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Lang |first1=Robert |date=September 3, 2026 |title=The 65 Movies That Have Made More Than $1 Billion At The Global Box Office |url=https://deadline.com/gallery/highest-grossing-movies-all-time/ |access-date=September 4, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |archive-date=September 4, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260904014621/https://deadline.com/gallery/highest-grossing-movies-all-time/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

===Ensemble roles===
{{Main|Captain America: Civil War|l1 = ''Captain America: Civil War''|Avengers: Infinity War|l2 = ''Avengers: Infinity War''|Avengers: Endgame|l3 = ''Avengers: Endgame''}}

''Captain America: Civil War'' marked Spider-Man's first appearance in the MCU.<ref name=sonywallstreet/><ref name="Spider-Man-Civil-War">{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2015/film/news/russo-brothers-sign-first-look-deal-with-sony-1201445430/|title=Russo Brothers Sign First-Look Deal with Sony|last=McNary|first=David|work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=March 3, 2015|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220415064028/https://variety.com/2015/film/news/russo-brothers-sign-first-look-deal-with-sony-1201445430/|archive-date=April 15, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> Filmmaking duo [[Russo brothers|Anthony and Joe Russo]] directed ''Civil War'', and they campaigned intensively to reintroduce the character in the film.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.indiewire.com/features/general/russo-brothers-spider-man-leaves-mcu-surprised-1202172201/|title=Russo Brothers React to Spider-Man Leaving MCU: ‘Not So Surprised or Devastated’|last=Sharf|first=Zack|work=[[IndieWire]]|date=September 9, 2019|access-date=January 26, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260126230014/https://www.indiewire.com/features/general/russo-brothers-spider-man-leaves-mcu-surprised-1202172201/|archive-date=January 26, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> Production for ''Civil War'' commenced in 2015, lasting four months.<ref name="IMAXCamera">{{Cite web |last=Lang |first=Brent |date=April 13, 2015 |title='Captain America: Civil War' First to Use New Imax/Arri 2D Camera (Exclusive) |url=https://variety.com/2015/film/news/captain-america-civil-war-first-to-use-new-imaxarri-2d-camera-exclusive-1201470965/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150414180557/http://variety.com/2015/film/news/captain-america-civil-war-first-to-use-new-imaxarri-2d-camera-exclusive-1201470965/ |archive-date=April 14, 2015 |access-date=April 13, 2015 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref><ref name="WrapCelebration">{{Cite magazine |last=Romano |first=Nick |date=August 22, 2015 |title=See the Captain America: Civil War cast celebrate wrapping production |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2015/08/22/captain-america-civil-war-filming-ends-cast-celebrates |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150824015935/http://www.ew.com/article/2015/08/22/captain-america-civil-war-filming-ends-cast-celebrates |archive-date=August 24, 2015 |access-date=August 23, 2015 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref>

Marvel produced two [[The Avengers (film series)|''Avengers'' films]] featuring Holland as Spider-Man: ''[[Avengers: Infinity War]]'' (2018) and ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]'' (2019).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/avengers-infinity-war-featurette-shows-first-footage-set-974673/|title='Avengers: Infinity War' Featurette Shows Off First Footage From Set|last=Couch|first=Aaron|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=February 10, 2017|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220320035223/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/avengers-infinity-war-featurette-shows-first-footage-set-974673/|archive-date=March 20, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="HollandAvengers4">{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/marvels-kevin-feige-why-studio-wont-make-r-movies-guardians-2-joss-whedons-dc-move-99507-995076/|title=Marvel's Kevin Feige on Why the Studio Won't Make R-Rated Movies, 'Guardians 2' and Joss Whedon's DC Move|last1=Kit|first1=Borys|last2=Couch|first2=Aaron|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=April 18, 2017|access-date=April 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220412125422/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/marvels-kevin-feige-why-studio-wont-make-r-movies-guardians-2-joss-whedons-dc-move-99507-995076/|archive-date=April 12, 2022|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Infinity War'' and ''Endgame'' were initially conceptualized as a [[List of films split into multiple parts|two-part film]], but the studios later split the project into two distinct films that they shot concurrently in 2017.<ref name="TwoPart">{{cite web |last1=Ryan |first1=Mike |title=Russo Brothers Confirm: 'Avengers: Infinity War 1 And 2' Will Be Retitled |url=https://uproxx.com/movies/russo-brothers-confirm-avengers-infinity-war-title-change/ |website=[[Uproxx]] |access-date=March 31, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230324131346/https://uproxx.com/movies/russo-brothers-confirm-avengers-infinity-war-title-change/ |archive-date=March 24, 2023 |date=May 4, 2016}}</ref><ref name="BacktoBack">{{Cite web |last=Schmidt |first=Joseph |date=January 22, 2017 |title=Avengers: Infinity War And Sequel Set To Begin Filming Monday |url=https://comicbook.com/marvel/2017/01/22/avengers-infinity-war-sequel-begin-filming/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170123143940/http://comicbook.com/marvel/2017/01/22/avengers-infinity-war-sequel-begin-filming/ |archive-date=January 23, 2017 |access-date=January 22, 2017 |website=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref>

==Animated ''Spider-Verse''==

===''Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse'' (2018)===
{{main|Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse {{!}} ''Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse''}}

[[File:Shameik Moore (53182794002).jpg|thumb|upright|alt=Cropped photo of Shameik Moore at the 2023 GalaxyCon Raleigh|[[Shameik Moore]] in 2023]]

Based off the failure of ''The Amazing Spider-Man 2'', Sony began planning spinoffs to rehabilitate the franchise, including an animated film.<ref name=sonywallstreet/> Pascal approached, then hired, the filmmakers [[Phil Lord and Christopher Miller]] for a co-production.<ref name="PascalInterview"/> Their concept gleans from the "[[Spider-Verse]]" story arc of ''The Amazing Spider-Man'' comics, featuring [[Miles Morales]], an alternate incarnation of Spider-Man from Marvel's [[Ultimate Marvel|Ultimate Comics]] imprint, as the main protagonist.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Galuppo |first=Mia |date=January 18, 2017 |title=Miles Morales Confirmed to Lead Sony Animation’s Spider-Man Feature |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/miles-morales-confirmed-lead-sony-animations-spider-man-feature-965525/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250905203611/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/miles-morales-confirmed-lead-sony-animations-spider-man-feature-965525/ |archive-date=September 5, 2025 |access-date=September 5, 2025 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last=McMillan|first=Graeme|title=Where ‘Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse’ Got Its Name|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/spider-man-spider-verse-comic-books-inspired-it-1066635/|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=December 11, 2017|access-date=September 5, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250905221703/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/spider-man-spider-verse-comic-books-inspired-it-1066635/|archive-date=September 5, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> 

Lord and [[Rodney Rothman]] prepared the ''Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse'' script, and the responsibility for directing was split between Rothman, [[Bob Persichetti]], and [[Peter Ramsey]].<ref name=emoji>{{cite news|last=Kit|first=Borys|title=Sony Unveils Plans for Animated 'Spider-Man' and 'Emojimovie: Express Yourself'|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/sony-unveils-plans-animated-spider-904574|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=June 20, 2016|access-date=June 20, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913023800/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/sony-unveils-plans-animated-spider-904574/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Title">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2017/12/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-first-look-trailer-unveiled-in-brazil-1202223495/|title='Spider-Man: Into The Spider-Verse' First Look Trailer Unveiled in Brazil|last=Haring|first=Bruce|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=December 9, 2017|access-date=September 5, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171209235651/https://deadline.com/2017/12/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-first-look-trailer-unveiled-in-brazil-1202223495/|archive-date=December 9, 2017| url-status = live }}</ref> Actor [[Shameik Moore]] stars as Miles, which was announced in the media in April 2017.<ref>{{cite news|last=Kit|first=Borys|title=Animated Spider-Man Film Finds Its Miles Morales (Exclusive)|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/animated-spider-man-film-finds-miles-morales-993317/|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=April 13, 2017|access-date=September 5, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250905222332/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/animated-spider-man-film-finds-miles-morales-993317/|archive-date=September 5, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Jake Johnson]], [[John Mulaney]], [[Nicolas Cage]], and [[Chris Pine]] voice Spider-Men from alternate universes.<ref>{{Cite web |last= Kohn |first=Erin |date=December 19, 2018 |title= ‘Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse’: Inside the Other Groundbreaking Marvel Blockbuster |url= https://www.indiewire.com/awards/industry/spider-man-into-the-spiderverse-diverse-cast-1202029412/ |url-status=live |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20250919205735/https://www.indiewire.com/awards/industry/spider-man-into-the-spiderverse-diverse-cast-1202029412/ |archive-date=September 19, 2025 |access-date=September 19, 2025 |website=[[IndieWire]]}}</ref><ref name="CageBogart">{{cite magazine|url=https://ew.com/movies/2018/08/15/spider-man-spider-verse-nicolas-cage/|title=Nicolas Cage based his Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse character on Humphrey Bogart|last=Collis|first=Clark|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|date=August 15, 2018|access-date=September 19, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180816034026/https://ew.com/movies/2018/08/15/spider-man-spider-verse-nicolas-cage/|archive-date=August 16, 2018| url-status = live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Schmidt |first=J.K. |date=November 29, 2018 |title='Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse' Features Chris Pine in a Surprising Cameo |url=https://comicbook.com/marvel/2018/11/29/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-chris-pine-cameo/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181130144328/https://comicbook.com/marvel/2018/11/29/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-chris-pine-cameo/ |archive-date=November 30, 2018 |access-date=September 19, 2025 |website=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref> The ''Spider-Verse'' timeline exists independently from the live-action Spider-Man films.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://variety.com/2015/film/news/spider-man-animated-movie-coming-in-2018-1201477933/|title='Spider-Man' Animated Movie Coming in 2018|author=<!-- Variety Staff -->|work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=April 22, 2015|access-date=September 5, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171211084420/http://variety.com/2015/film/news/spider-man-animated-movie-coming-in-2018-1201477933/|archive-date=December 11, 2017| url-status = live }}</ref> After its December 2018 release,<ref>{{cite news|url=https://variety.com/2018/film/news/box-office-spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-mortal-engines-flops-1203090895/|title=Box Office: ‘Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse’ Swings to $35 Million Debut, ‘Mortal Engines’ Sputters|first=Rebecca|last=Rubin|work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=December 16, 2018|access-date=January 25, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240930141310/https://variety.com/2018/film/news/box-office-spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-mortal-engines-flops-1203090895/|archive-date=September 30, 2024| url-status = live }}</ref> ''Into the Spider-Verse'' became the first non-Disney film to win the [[Academy Award for Best Animated Feature]] in seven years.<ref>{{cite web|last=Marrow|first=Brendan|date=February 24, 2019|title=Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse becomes the first non-Disney film to win the animation Oscar in 7 years.|url=https://theweek.com/speedreads/825502/spiderman-into-spiderverse-becomes-first-nondisney-film-win-animation-oscar-7-years|work=[[The Week]]|access-date=September 20, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190225111006/https://theweek.com/speedreads/825502/spiderman-into-spiderverse-becomes-first-nondisney-film-win-animation-oscar-7-years|archive-date=February 25, 2019}}</ref>

===''Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse'' (2023)===
{{main|Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse {{!}} ''Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse''}}

Studio discussions for a sequel, ''Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse'', preceded the release of ''Into the Spider-Verse''.<ref name="Nov2018Plans3">{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2018/film/news/sony-spider-man-into-the-spiderverse-sequels-spinoffs-1203037792/|title=Sony Developing 'Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse' Sequel and Spinoff|last=McNary|first=Dave|work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=November 27, 2018|access-date=November 30, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181128000434/https://variety.com/2018/film/news/sony-spider-man-into-the-spiderverse-sequels-spinoffs-1203037792/|archive-date=November 28, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Across the Spider-Verse'' originated from a planned two-part film that was revised once the filmmakers developed the story to indicate a separate follow-up film.<ref>{{cite web|last=Butkovic|first=Leanne|title=Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse Directors, Writer on the Decision to Split It Into Two Parts|work=[[IGN]]|date=May 24, 2023|url=https://www.ign.com/articles/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-directors-writer-on-the-decision-to-split-it-into-two-parts|access-date=September 9, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250908161100/https://www.ign.com/articles/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-directors-writer-on-the-decision-to-split-it-into-two-parts|archive-date=September 8, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Lord and Miller returned to undertake the scriptwriting with [[David Callaham]], based on a plot depicting a romance between Miles and [[Gwen Stacy (Spider-Verse)|Gwen Stacy / Spider-Woman]] ([[Hailee Steinfeld]]).<ref>{{cite web| first1=Phil |last1=Lord | first2=Christopher | last2=Miller |url= https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/awards/story/2024-02-12/writing-across-spider-verse-chris-miller-phil-lord |title=With ‘Spider-Man,’ how do you top a winner? Try doing the opposite |work= [[Los Angeles Times]] |date=February 12, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250909141255/https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/awards/story/2024-02-12/writing-across-spider-verse-chris-miller-phil-lord |archive-date= September 9, 2025|access-date=September 9, 2025}}</ref><ref name="PascalDec2018">{{Cite web |last=Robinson |first=Joanna |date=December 14, 2018 |title=Sony Finally Untangles Its Spider Web |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2018/12/sony-spider-man-future-amy-pascal-phil-lord-interview |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181214201718/https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2018/12/sony-spider-man-future-amy-pascal-phil-lord-interview |archive-date=December 14, 2018 |access-date=September 9, 2025 |website=[[Vanity Fair (magazine)|Vanity Fair]]}}</ref> Sony engaged [[Joaquim Dos Santos]], [[Kemp Powers]] and [[Justin K. Thompson]] to direct ''Across the Spider-Verse''.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Vary|first=Adam B.|date=April 19, 2021|title='Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse' Sequel Snares New Directing Trio (EXCLUSIVE)|url=https://variety.com/2021/film/news/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-2-directors-1234951631/|access-date=April 19, 2021|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913025015/https://variety.com/2021/film/news/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-2-directors-1234951631/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> The film is distinguished with an expanded cast of Spider-People, led by Johnson, [[Oscar Isaac]], [[Issa Rae]], [[Daniel Kaluuya]], and [[Karan Soni]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.polygon.com/23505869/spider-man-across-spider-verse-characters-cast/|title=Every Spider-Man cameo in Across the Spider-Verse, explained|first=Zach|last=Rabiroff|date=June 2, 2023|website=[[polygon (website)|Polygon]]|access-date=November 3, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250808171001/https://www.polygon.com/23505869/spider-man-across-spider-verse-characters-cast/|archive-date=August 8, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last1=Mendez II |first1=Moises |last2=McCluskey |first2=Megan |date=June 2, 2023 |title=A Handy Guide to All the Key Spider-People in Spider-Man: Across The Spider-Verse |url=https://time.com/6284549/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-spider-people/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250623063141/https://time.com/6284549/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-spider-people/|access-date=November 3, 2025 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]]|archive-date=June 23, 2025}}</ref> Production was mired in labor disputes.<ref name="VultureBadCondition">{{Cite web |last=Lee |first=Chris |date=June 23, 2023 |title=''Spider-Verse'' Artists Say Working on the Sequel Was 'Death by a Thousand Paper Cuts' |url=https://www.vulture.com/2023/06/spider-verse-animation-four-artists-on-making-the-sequel.html |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230623135356/https://www.vulture.com/2023/06/spider-verse-animation-four-artists-on-making-the-sequel.html |archive-date=June 23, 2023 |access-date=September 9, 2025 |website=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]] |quote=Multiple Across the Spider-Verse crew members... describe the process of making the $150{{nbsp}}million Sony project as uniquely arduous...}}</ref> After a delay in the release schedule, ''Across the Spider-Verse'' opened to theaters in June 2023,<ref name="theverge.com">{{Cite web|url=https://www.theverge.com/2019/11/1/20944354/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-sequel-april-2022-release-date-miles-morales|title=Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse sequel arrives April 2022|first=Julia|last=Alexander|date=November 1, 2019|website=[[The Verge]]|access-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913025526/https://www.theverge.com/2019/11/1/20944354/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-sequel-april-2022-release-date-miles-morales|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="421Shift">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony|date=April 21, 2022 |title='Spider-Man: Across The Spider-Verse' Heads To Summer 2023; Sony Dates 'Madame Web', 'Equalizer 3' Among Other Release Changes |url=https://deadline.com/2022/04/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-summer-2023-theatrical-release-sony-release-date-changes-1235007010/ |access-date=April 21, 2022 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913030118/https://deadline.com/2022/04/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-summer-2023-theatrical-release-sony-release-date-changes-1235007010/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> finishing the year as the [[2023 in film#Highest-grossing films|sixth highest-grossing film]] with $690.9 million.<ref>{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=May 3, 2024 |title='Spider-Man: Across The Spider-Verse' Conquers Superhero Fatigue At No. 3 In Deadline's 2023 Most Valuable Blockbuster Tournament |url=https://deadline.com/2024/05/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-movie-profits-1235902863/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240608203358/https://deadline.com/2024/05/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-movie-profits-1235902863/ |archive-date=June 8, 2024 |access-date=September 18, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> As well, the film was a candidate for Best Animated Feature at the [[96th Academy Awards]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nordyke |first=Kimberly |date=March 10, 2024 |title=Oscars: Full List of Winners |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/oscars-2024-winners-list-1235847823/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240311030812/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/oscars-2024-winners-list-1235847823/ |archive-date=March 11, 2024 |access-date=September 19, 2025 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref>

===''Spider-Man: Beyond the Spider-Verse'' (2027)===
{{Main|Spider-Man: Beyond the Spider-Verse {{!}} ''Spider-Man: Beyond the Spider-Verse''}}

Creation of ''Spider-Man: Beyond the Spider-Verse'' coincided with ''Across the Spider-Verse''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Butkovic |first=Leanne |date=May 24, 2023 |title=Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse Directors, Writer on the Decision to Split It Into Two Parts |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-directors-writer-on-the-decision-to-split-it-into-two-parts |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251002095853/https://www.ign.com/articles/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-directors-writer-on-the-decision-to-split-it-into-two-parts |archive-date=October 2, 2025 |access-date=January 25, 2026 |website=[[IGN]]}}</ref> Sony originally scheduled a March 29, 2024 release date for ''Beyond the Spider-Verse'', but postponed the film indefinitely in the wake of the [[2023 SAG-AFTRA strike]].<ref name="421Shift"/><ref name="IndefiniteDelayBTSV">{{Cite web |last=Donnelly |first=Matt |date=July 28, 2023 |title='Beyond the Spider-Verse' Taken Off Sony Release Calendar as Strikes Delay 'Kraven' and 'Ghostbusters' Sequel to 2024 |url=https://variety.com/2023/film/news/spider-man-beyond-the-spider-verse-kraven-release-date-pushed-2024-strikes-1235682520/ |access-date=July 28, 2023 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913030619/https://variety.com/2023/film/news/spider-man-beyond-the-spider-verse-kraven-release-date-pushed-2024-strikes-1235682520/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> The studio plans to release the film on June 18, 2027.<ref name="2027ReleaseForward">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=September 25, 2025 |title=''Spider-Man: Beyond The Spider-Verse'' Swings Onto Pixar's ''Gatto'' Father's Day Weekend 2027 |url=https://deadline.com/2025/09/spider-man-beyond-the-spider-verse-release-date-1236462687/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250925003227/https://deadline.com/2025/09/spider-man-beyond-the-spider-verse-release-date-1236462687/ |archive-date=September 25, 2025 |access-date=September 25, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>

===Spin-offs===
{{Main|Spider-Ham: Caught in a Ham {{!}} ''Spider-Ham: Caught in a Ham''|The Spider Within: A Spider-Verse Story {{!}} ''The Spider Within: A Spider-Verse Story''}}

Due to the success of the ''Spider-Verse'', development is ongoing on spinoffs that explore the mythology of Spider-Man.<ref name="PascalDec2018"/> The completed projects take the form of short films. The first, ''[[Spider-Ham: Caught in a Ham]]'', was released in tandem with ''Into the Spider-Verse''{{'s}} digital launch on February 26, 2019, featuring Mulaney reprising his role as [[Spider-Ham]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Coogan |first1=Devan |title=Exclusive: Watch a clip from Spider-Ham's new 'Spider-Verse' short |url=https://ew.com/movies/2019/02/18/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-home-release-spider-ham-short/ |access-date=February 18, 2019 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |date=February 18, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913031648/https://ew.com/movies/2019/02/18/spider-man-into-the-spider-verse-home-release-spider-ham-short/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live|language=en}}</ref> On the other hand, ''[[The Spider Within: A Spider-Verse Story]]'' premiered at the [[Annecy International Animation Film Festival]] in France in June 2023 and later on [[YouTube]] in March 2024.<ref name=spiderversestorydeadline>{{Cite web |last=Goodfellow |first=Melanie |date=June 12, 2023 |title=Sony Unveils First Look At Spider-Verse Short Film Tackling Mental Issues & Showing Miles Morales Suffering An Anxiety Crisis – Annecy |url=https://deadline.com/2023/06/sony-pictures-animation-the-spider-within-a-spider-verse-story-annecy-1235414400/ |access-date=June 12, 2023 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913032043/https://deadline.com/2023/06/sony-pictures-animation-the-spider-within-a-spider-verse-story-annecy-1235414400/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2024/artisans/news/spider-verse-animated-short-the-spider-within-1235948300/ |title='Spider-Verse' Animated Short to Debut on YouTube From Sony Pictures in Partnership With the Kevin Love Fund (EXCLUSIVE) |website=Variety |first=Jazz |last=Tangcay |date=March 21, 2024 |access-date=March 21, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913032716/https://variety.com/2024/artisans/news/spider-verse-animated-short-the-spider-within-1235948300/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> ''A Spider-Verse Story'' depicts Miles undergoing a [[panic attack]] induced by stress in his personal life.<ref name=spiderversestorydeadline/>

Among the upcoming projects are a Spider-Women spinoff and a [[Spider-Punk]] adaptation.<ref name="PascalDec2018"/><ref name="Spider-VerseSequelPlans2027"/><ref name=spiderpunk>{{Cite web |last=Grobar |first=Matt |date=August 5, 2025 |title=Spider-Punk Animated Feature From Daniel Kaluuya & Ajon Singh In Development At Sony |url=https://deadline.com/2025/08/spider-punk-animated-feature-daniel-kaluuya-ajon-singh-sony-1236478287/ |access-date=August 5, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913033422/https://deadline.com/2025/08/spider-punk-animated-feature-daniel-kaluuya-ajon-singh-sony-1236478287/|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live |language=en-US}}</ref> Kaluuya is writing the script for the Spider-Punk film with Ajon Singh.<ref name=spiderpunk/> The premise of the Spider-Women spinoff will be a Gwen-centric narrative introducing [[Silk (character)|Cindy Moon / Silk]] and [[Spider-Woman (Jessica Drew)|Jessica Drew / Spider-Woman]] onscreen.<ref name="Spider-VerseSequelPlans2027">{{cite web|url=https://www.superherohype.com/movies/430257-amy-pascal-teases-into-the-spider-verse-sequel-plans-new-characters|title=Amy Pascal Teases Into the Spider-Verse Sequel Plans, New Characters|last=Abbate|first=Jake|publisher=SuperHeroHype|date=December 14, 2018|access-date=December 15, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913034054/https://www.superherohype.com/movies/430257-amy-pascal-teases-into-the-spider-verse-sequel-plans-new-characters|archive-date=September 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> In May 2023, reports emerged that Sony was contemplating a live-action Miles Morales film, which would take priority after the releases of ''Brand New Day'' and ''Beyond the Spider-Verse''.<ref name="PascalMay2023">{{Cite magazine |last=Malkin |first=Marc |date=May 31, 2023 |title=''Spider-Man'' Producers Tease Live-Action Miles Morales Movie and Animated ''Spider-Woman'' Film: 'It's All Happening' |url=https://variety.com/2023/film/columns/across-the-spider-verse-miles-morales-spider-woman-1235629183/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230531204208/https://variety.com/2023/film/columns/across-the-spider-verse-miles-morales-spider-woman-1235629183/ |archive-date=May 31, 2023 |access-date=May 31, 2023 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref><ref name="PascalMillerFeb2024">{{Cite web |last=Barnhardt |first=Adam |date=February 12, 2024 |title=Live-Action Miles Morales Movie Teased by ''Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse'' Producer |url=https://comicbook.com/movies/news/miles-morales-live-action-movie-teased-chris-miller-spider-verse/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240224183726/https://comicbook.com/movies/news/miles-morales-live-action-movie-teased-chris-miller-spider-verse/ |archive-date=February 24, 2024 |access-date=February 24, 2024 |website=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref>

==Sony's Spider-Man Universe==
{{main|Sony's Spider-Man Universe}}

Since 2018, Sony has distributed a series of live-action films based on secondary characters of the Spider-Man canon, part of a broader multimedia project dubbed [[Sony's Spider-Man Universe]] (SSU).<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://variety.com/2018/film/news/whats-next-for-the-spider-man-universe-after-venom-exclusive-1202900203/ |title=What’s Next for the Spider-Man Universe After ‘Venom’ (EXCLUSIVE) |last1=Lang |first1=Brent |last2=Kroll |first2=Justin |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |date=September 27, 2019 |access-date=September 27, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190927160452/https://variety.com/2019/film/news/sony-marvel-tom-holland-spider-man-1203351489/ |archive-date=September 27, 2019 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Warner |first=Sam |date=August 25, 2021 |title=Sony's Marvel universe has been given another rebrand |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/movies/a37394142/sony-marvel-spider-man-universe-movies/|url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250502232522/https://www.digitalspy.com/movies/a37394142/sony-marvel-spider-man-universe-movies/ |archive-date=May 2, 2025 |access-date=January 25, 2026 |website=[[Digital Spy]]}}</ref> The franchise's first entry is ''[[Venom (2018 film)|Venom]]'' (2018), itself comprising a trilogy with ''[[Venom: Let There Be Carnage]]'' (2021) and ''[[Venom: The Last Dance]]'' (2024).<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Murphy |first=Katcy |date=March 12, 2024 |title=‘Venom 3’ Is Titled ‘Venom: The Last Dance’; Tom Hardy Sequel Moves Up to October Date |url=https://variety.com/2024/film/news/venom-3-title-last-dance-release-date-tom-hardy-1235940273/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240313002953/https://variety.com/2024/film/news/venom-3-title-last-dance-release-date-tom-hardy-1235940273/ |archive-date=March 13, 2024 |access-date=September 11, 2025 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Three other titles complete the SSU: ''[[Morbius (film)|Morbius]]'' (2022), ''[[Madame Web (film)|Madame Web]]'', and ''[[Kraven the Hunter (film)|Kraven the Hunter]]'' (both 2024).<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Vary |first=Adam B. |date=December 13, 2024 |title=Even After ‘Kraven the Hunter’ and ‘Madame Web,’ Sony’s Marvel Movies Aren’t Dead (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2024/film/news/kraven-sony-marvel-movies-not-dead-1236249221/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250911163314/https://variety.com/2024/film/news/kraven-sony-marvel-movies-not-dead-1236249221/ |archive-date=September 11, 2025 |access-date=September 11, 2025 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Sony ceased their output of films indefinitely after the box office failures of ''Madame Web'' and ''Kraven the Hunter''.<ref name="TheWrapFinalBow">{{Cite web |last=Gonzalez |first=Umberto |date=December 10, 2024 |title=As ''Kraven'' Hunts for Audience, Sony's Marvel Universe Takes Final Bow for Now {{!}} Analysis |url=https://www.thewrap.com/kraven-the-hunter-sony-marvel-universe-spider-man-box-office/ |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241210152025/https://www.thewrap.com/kraven-the-hunter-sony-marvel-universe-spider-man-box-office/ |archive-date=December 10, 2024 |access-date=September 11, 2025 |website=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref> The SSU operates with a loosely shared continuity to all existing Spider-Man film franchises but does not explicitly feature the character beyond the depiction of Peter's birth in ''Madame Web''.{{efn|Attributed to multiple sources:<ref name="NWHSMTASM">{{Cite web |last=Debruge |first=Peter |date=December 13, 2021 |title='Spider-Man: No Way Home' Review: Tom Holland Cleans Out the Cobwebs of Sprawling Franchise With Multiverse Super-Battle |url=https://variety.com/2021/film/reviews/spider-man-no-way-home-review-tom-holland-1235132550/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211214115857/https://variety.com/2021/film/reviews/spider-man-no-way-home-review-tom-holland-1235132550/ |archive-date=December 14, 2021 |access-date=September 11, 2025 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref><ref name="SSUNWH">{{Cite web |last=Sandwell |first=Ian |date=December 15, 2021 |title=Spider-Man: No Way Home credits scene explained |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/movies/a38512270/spider-man-no-way-home-venom-eddie-brock-explained-credits-scene/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211216051600/https://www.digitalspy.com/movies/a38512270/spider-man-no-way-home-venom-eddie-brock-explained-credits-scene/ |archive-date=December 16, 2021 |access-date=September 11, 2025 |website=[[Digital Spy]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Newby |first=Richard |date=April 1, 2022 |title=It's a Bird! It's a Bat! It's Morbius's Mid-Credits Scenes, Explained |url=https://www.vulture.com/2022/04/morbius-post-credits-scenes-with-vulture-explained.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250828173222/https://www.vulture.com/2022/04/morbius-post-credits-scenes-with-vulture-explained.html|archive-date=August 28, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=September 11, 2025 |website=Vulture |language=en-us}}</ref><ref name="AcrossSpiderVerse">{{Cite magazine |last=Gvozden |first=Dan |date=June 4, 2023 |title=The Definitive List of 'Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse' Easter Eggs |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-easter-eggs-list-1235506838/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230605002218/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/spider-man-across-the-spider-verse-easter-eggs-list-1235506838/ |archive-date=June 5, 2023 |access-date=September 11, 2025 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref name="SpideyConnectionsTime">{{Cite magazine |last=Grebey |first=James |date=February 14, 2024 |title=How ''Madame Web'' Connects to the Spider-Man Cinematic Multiverse |url=https://time.com/6694571/how-madame-web-relates-to-spider-man/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240215013648/https://time.com/6694571/how-madame-web-relates-to-spider-man/ |archive-date=February 15, 2024 |access-date=February 15, 2024 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]]}}</ref>}}

==Amateur works==

Amateur films about Spider-Man examine a range of interpretations of the character from ordinary people.{{sfn|Peaslee|Weiner|2016|p=4}} [[Donald F. Glut]] produced the [[Spider-Man (1969 film)|earliest known Spider-Man fan film in 1969]], featuring the character battling in a California state park.{{sfn|Young|2008|p=38–39}} It was Glut's final amateur film before pursuing an acting career.{{sfn|Young|2008|p=38–39}} ''[[Spider-Man Versus Kraven the Hunter]]'' (1974) was director Bruce Cardozo's student project for his studies at [[New York University]]'s [[Tisch School of the Arts]].{{sfn|Young|2008|p=50}} Lee, impressed by the film's scope, permitted its noncommercial exhibition, but refused Cardozo's proposals for a theatrical release because they did not share the same vision for a feature film.{{sfn|Young|2008|p=51–53}} ''Spider-Man Versus Kraven the Hunter'' chronicles [[Kraven the Hunter]]'s pursuit to kill Spider-Man in a conspiracy devised by ''[[Daily Bugle]]'' publisher [[J. Jonah Jameson]].{{sfn|Young|2008|p=51–53}} The film has seldom been shown since its release.{{sfn|Young|2008|p=58}} James Krieg's ''[[Viva Spider-Man]]'' (1989) attempts to reimagine [[Spider-Man (1967 TV series)|the first animated TV adaptation of Spider-Man]].{{sfn|Nery|2017|p=131}} 

In 1992, Dan Poole developed ''[[The Green Goblin's Last Stand]]'' as an adaptation of ''The Amazing Spider-Man''{{'s}} "[[The Night Gwen Stacy Died]]" storyline.{{sfn|Young|2008|p=127–130}} Poole financed the film's $400 budget with wages from his job as a mail clerk at the [[National Aquarium (Baltimore)|National Aquarium]] in Baltimore.{{sfn|Young|2008|p=127–130}}<ref>
{{Cite news|first=Maurice |last=Martin |title=Web Master |format=reprint |work=[[Baltimore City Paper]] |date=May 1, 2002 |accessdate=November 14, 2025 |url=http://www.mauricemartin.net/spider.htm |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20080701010924/http://www.mauricemartin.net/spider.htm |archivedate=July 1, 2008 }}</ref> He also performed most of the stunt work in ''The Green Goblin's Last Stand'', including a simulated web slinging sequence that was recorded at an unoccupied office building.{{sfn|Young|2008|p=127–130}} Other unauthorized depictions of Spider-Man include the [[Turksploitation|Turkish exploitation film]] ''[[3 Dev Adam]]'' ({{lit|3 Giant Men}}, 1973), featuring the character as the mastermind of a counterfeiting scheme, and ''[[Dariya Dil]]'' (1988).{{sfnm|1a1=Glaser|1y=2022|1p=9|2a1=Peaslee|2a2=Weiner|2y=2016|2p=4}}

Production of amateur Spider-Man films has continued into the twenty-first century. ''[[Italian Spiderman]]'' (2007), a short film released in snippets on [[YouTube]], parodies Italian adventure films of the mid-twentieth century, though it bears little resemblance to the American comics.{{sfn|Peaslee|Weiner|2016|p=4}} ''[[Spider-Man: Lotus]]'' (2023) depicts a story partially shaped by director Gavin J. Konop's struggles as a high school student.<ref name=lotus/> Konop crowdfunded $112,000 for the budget through [[Indiegogo]] and released the film in August 2023.<ref name=lotus>{{Cite news |title=A Fan Made a Spider-Man Film. The Fallout Has Been Unexpected. |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=August 23, 2023 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/23/movies/spider-man-lotus-fan-film.html |access-date=November 13, 2025 |url-access=subscription |first=Christopher |last=Kuo |archive-date=August 26, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250826043743/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/23/movies/spider-man-lotus-fan-film.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=dblotus>{{cite news|url=https://www.thedailybeast.com/obsessed/spider-man-lotus-review-scandal-plagued-fanmade-film-is-a-mess/|title=‘Spider-Man: Lotus’: Scandal-Plagued Fanmade Film Is a Mess|work=[[The Daily Beast]]|date=August 15, 2023|access-date=November 13, 2025|last1=Frank|first1=Allegra|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250321013408/https://www.thedailybeast.com/obsessed/spider-man-lotus-review-scandal-plagued-fanmade-film-is-a-mess/|archive-date=March 21, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Lotus'' was derided by fans, and leaked texts of racist comments sent by Konop and lead actor Warden Wayne drew widespread coverage in the media.<ref name=lotus/><ref name=dblotus/>

