=== Theatrical re-releases ===

In March 2024, Sony spearheaded a re-release campaign of the live-action Spider-Man films to commemorate Columbia's [[centennial]] anniversary.<ref name="Columbia100th">{{Cite web |last=Scott |first=Ryan |date=March 18, 2024 |title=Every Spider-Man Movie Is Returning To Theaters To Help Save The Box Office (And Sony)|url=https://www.slashfilm.com/1542498/every-spider-man-movie-returning-to-theaters-help-save-box-office/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240413141937/https://www.slashfilm.com/1542498/every-spider-man-movie-returning-to-theaters-help-save-box-office/ |archive-date=April 13, 2024 |access-date=January 26, 2026|website=[[SlashFilm|/Film]]}}</ref> They commenced the theatrical rollout with the Raimi trilogy in April, followed by ''The Amazing Spider-Man'' films in mid-May, before concluding with the MCU trilogy in multiple weekends from late May to early June.<ref name="Columbia100th"/> Sony again screened the Raimi trilogy in a two-weekend release campaign in late 2025, part of a joint venture with [[Fathom Events]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Murphy |first=J. Kim |date=June 26, 2025 |title=‘Spider-Man’ Original Trilogy Returning to Theaters From Fathom Entertainment: Re-Release Includes 2.1 Extended Cut|url=https://variety.com/2025/film/news/spider-man-trilogy-rereleasing-theaters-21-extended-cut-1236441228/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250912153151/https://variety.com/2025/film/news/spider-man-trilogy-rereleasing-theaters-21-extended-cut-1236441228/ |archive-date=September 12, 2025 |access-date=September 12, 2025 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref>

